# Audio is what makes this repository heavy: sound/ accounts for roughly 1.4 GB
# of history against about 280 MB for every sprite in the game. The NOX_SOUND
# library alone is ~1 GB of uncompressed WAV, and a sample of it found under
# one file in eight referenced by any scene or script.
#
# Tracking them here keeps *new* audio out of git history. It does not move what
# is already committed — that needs a history rewrite:
#
#   git lfs install --local
#   git lfs migrate import --include="*.wav" --everything
#   git push --force origin --all
#
# Anything cloned before that rewrite has to be re-cloned.
*.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ogg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp3 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Godot's own text formats must stay diffable, so they are deliberately absent
# from the list above, as are the .import sidecars that carry each asset's UID.
